#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:14 4d028d38dcfa4c40944c988fad0c1472
msgid "Appendix E — Publishing a Bilingual Knowledge Base"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:16 47ca01e2f83a4770b7094b6e00936710
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Scope. This appendix is deliberately document-only and self-contained. It"
" describes the bilingual publishing discipline the author has refined in "
"a private project-knowledge-base toolkit {cite}`fanyamin_pkb_skill` and "
"adapts it to the `sphinx + myst` toolchain this book is built with. It "
"does not wire new `make` targets; use the existing `make book-i18n` / "
"`make book-build` targets from this book's Makefile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:24 03b9ef684bae47ebb52941e3d8e3fbf1
msgid "Why publish bilingually"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:26 4a34a276b3fd407a8a72fe8b9d765187
msgid ""
"A knowledge base written in only the author's first language excludes "
"readers who are fluent in their second or third language but cannot read "
"the first at professional depth. A KB written in only English excludes "
"the large fraction of a Chinese-speaking engineering team that prefers "
"Chinese for technical depth (and vice versa). The choice is not *which* "
"language but *which discipline for keeping two languages in sync without "
"doubling the authoring cost*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:34 77d87d9032b44f3c899905a2657c2bd3
msgid "Three failure modes make this harder than it looks:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:36 fffbdbcf7291401d9f5df32d44d801f2
msgid ""
"**Translation drift.** An English page is updated; the Chinese "
"translation is not. The Chinese reader sees a stale page that looks "
"current."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:39 9ebb7bbdffe641969790dd4c776d254e
msgid ""
"**Anchor drift.** An English H2 heading is reworded; the Chinese "
"translation still carries the old anchor. Cross-document links break "
"silently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:42 4063021def824db88e1d47e400c15ac7
msgid ""
"**Source-of-truth drift.** Two parallel prose files exist; each gets "
"edited independently; the two languages diverge in content, not just in "
"wording."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:46 e5ed743cf77b4bdaa547b2b0a4398cf1
msgid ""
"The Sphinx toolchain plus a small amount of discipline addresses all "
"three."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:49 0cdd0d70bdbc4fbf943912cf569498f9
msgid "What the bilingual pipeline looks like"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:51 6b09e7720d384d4b9016ad412aa30822
msgid "One source language, multiple translation targets, one build per language:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:65 e2f73220fddc43c39cdcda50f60f6817
msgid ""
"The `.po` files are gettext message catalogues. Each catalogue entry "
"pairs one English string (the `msgid`) with one translated string (the "
"`msgstr`). Sphinx extracts the `msgid`s at build time; a translator "
"(human or machine) fills in the `msgstr`s; Sphinx re-renders HTML for "
"each target language from the same source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:71 70741efdc6f64233806960e4cc49d775
msgid ""
"The English prose remains the source of truth. The Chinese pages are "
"*rendered*, not maintained. This is the critical move: a KB with two "
"equal sources becomes a KB with two sources of drift."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:75 bef13c755d0b4549b815ea3499f7f881
msgid "How to make it reliable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:77 f2cd68535d0240c29ca33ef688c2559e
msgid "Four pieces of discipline, each cheap:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:79 3c51e4ca3e944fdfa5879f8b34ef5734
msgid "1. Turn on `gettext_uuid`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:81 141623a18a274987895f8f2b926aca58
msgid ""
"Without UUIDs, every translation entry is keyed by the English string "
"itself. Reword \"The retrieval layer consults the tuple\" to \"The "
"retriever reads the tuple,\" and the translation becomes orphaned: the "
"old entry points at prose that no longer exists; the new entry has no "
"translation. The translator must re-translate from scratch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:88 404f8f7a241a460cb191f4b18418a617
msgid ""
"With `gettext_uuid = True` in `conf.py`, each entry gets a stable UUID "
"the first time it appears. Rewording the English leaves the UUID intact; "
"the Chinese translation follows the UUID, not the string. In `conf.py`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:99 6da11ab6cf0d4103a7dcc9fff7692264
msgid ""
"The result: an English edit that preserves meaning preserves its "
"translation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:102
#: 99b4ad4ebef14c45bce77508570f2b60
msgid "2. Keep `.po` edits mechanical"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:104
#: fc4f73cffe30425697d76e84e5a0f250
msgid ""
"Editing `.po` files by hand is tedious and error-prone (a stray quote "
"breaks the file). Use `polib` for programmatic edits:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:120
#: 85c152707ed1433295c0906d1842aa14
msgid "Two rules make this safe:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:122
#: c94b883cb5614ce5a9b94c52a202360c
msgid ""
"**Every machine translation lands as `fuzzy`.** This is the gettext "
"convention: a fuzzy entry is shown to the reader untranslated (or as the "
"English fallback) until a human reviews and removes the flag. It mirrors "
"the \"AI always sets pending\" rule from Chapter 5 for frontmatter "
"footers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:127
#: 124e60e304494fe9b7931ab72dc346de
msgid ""
"**Never delete a translated entry because its `msgid` changed.** Let "
"`sphinx-intl update` handle it; the updater marks entries `fuzzy` when "
"the English string has drifted, which preserves prior work and signals "
"review."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:132
#: 7c9c8d9b801d4b67ba3e5bd809a96efd
msgid "3. Translate H1s through a hook"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:134
#: ebb3748a74094fdc8633377050b9be9d
msgid ""
"Sphinx's default behaviour renders the document title from the "
"frontmatter `title:` field, which is English. For Chinese output the "
"reader expects a Chinese title. A small `conf.py` hook handles this "
"without duplicating prose:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:160
#: 5d15b3c604ba437497a58a915ddfe21f
msgid ""
"The `h1_map.zh_CN.yml` is a small flat file the author maintains "
"alongside the prose:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:169
#: a19a3f34646047a5973cbacaa621c969
msgid ""
"This is more work than letting `.po` catalogues carry the titles, but it "
"produces a navigation sidebar that reads natively in each language — "
"which is the first thing a reader notices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:173
#: 13eb3ad6138042e1892d1eff911d11c4
msgid "4. Fail the build on untranslated critical pages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:175
#: f3e96f2c73c44be7ad2169199e9a64e1
msgid ""
"Not every chapter needs same-day Chinese. Runbooks do; an overview "
"chapter might lag by a week. Encode this in the frontmatter:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:185
#: e7d148e5bfc44c4badd551ce34407e9a
msgid "A one-line check at build time enforces the policy:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:196
#: 3555337e57264cfca53c9a1499e4c3b8
msgid ""
"Three values — `required`, `optional`, `none` — give every page an "
"explicit translation SLA. Operationally this mirrors the hard/soft gate "
"split from Chapter 15: `required` is a hard gate that blocks publish; "
"`optional` is a soft warning; `none` is silent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:201
#: e7da66f5ed434db2afd80917f0117aee
msgid "Example — one page through the pipeline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:203
#: dab7583c18fe434a9a08916a95452efe
msgid ""
"The lifecycle of `ch07a-prose-operational-model.md` through one editing "
"round:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:206
#: b1859cabfb874a3993d39c115fcb70d6
msgid "Author edits the English source. Reword a section heading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:207
#: e8e3a17faa614be9906c7c20f1d42c2b
msgid ""
"`make book-i18n` runs `sphinx-build -b gettext` + `sphinx-intl update`. "
"The UUID of the reworded heading is preserved; its Chinese translation is"
" now marked `fuzzy`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:210
#: f1bc5048dc3c4784a2396b5f8aa13a05
msgid ""
"`make book-build` builds English. Build succeeds; `zh_status` is "
"`optional` on this chapter, so the build does not fail on the fuzzy "
"entry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:213
#: 74926fa007ad4a7787d9604b29f9527b
msgid ""
"A bounded-LLM translation pass (analogous to Chapter 16's L2) generates a"
" new `msgstr` for the reworded heading and writes it back with the "
"`fuzzy` flag retained."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:216
#: a709809acc894a93bebf11a94bc10644
msgid ""
"A human reviewer opens the `.po` file in a PO-aware editor (Poedit, "
"Lokalize), reads the new Chinese text against the English, and removes "
"the `fuzzy` flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:219
#: 30f1446c0fa24f17801704155bdadcac
msgid ""
"Next `make book-build -D language=zh_CN` produces the Chinese HTML with "
"the approved translation in place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:222
#: 0f9232a9e9014e6eaa4a1c4609fdbe90
msgid ""
"Six steps, three of which are mechanical (`make` targets), two of which "
"are bounded LLM work (one translation call per changed entry), and one of"
" which is human review on a single diff. The total cost per English edit "
"is cents of LLM tokens plus a minute of human time per chapter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:228
#: 9b00d639f6f84154bdf9bf6e90d2dd0a
msgid "Operational failure modes and fixes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md da06c3c46d2f48efa87f7e02fb1608d9
msgid "Failure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md edda77e6f94a4b2b9b452888d8ead625
msgid "Symptom"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md 3f7b80368bd443d5ad8eb12d8a387e8f
msgid "Fix"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md f8e814071c194776b3ba5cd0ec2a1add
msgid "UUID disabled retroactively"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md 832bd53d9f634f97835640e5473689f0
msgid "Mass re-translation after a casual edit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md 08c5a8c39e2c4566845333d1c33077cc
msgid ""
"Turn on `gettext_uuid` *before* first translation pass; once on, leave it"
" on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md f83f150a075f4f35adf6da07b92ede62
msgid "`.po` edited by hand, syntax broken"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md 30f639af979f4213b1a1c7ad6e49fdc6
msgid "Sphinx fails with \"malformed entry near line N\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md 92e5aeee0c6e4445b47ea6f362e350da
msgid ""
"Always edit via `polib`; keep a pre-commit hook that runs `msgfmt "
"--check` on every `.po` file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md 7aafcfa2124b48eab44e7dd43b91150a
msgid "Translation lags English indefinitely"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md 5bcf1da35cab41cba56c2acf64849eed
msgid "Chinese readers see stale prose with no warning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md 83ded9156c3147498f856be37b37ac5b
msgid ""
"`zh_status: required` on critical pages; CI hard-fails when the coverage "
"drops below threshold."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md 2940565c19e34359a1bd2f8aaa3b3d56
msgid "Translator translates the prose but not the heading"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md 522434d8059543c88648a3a13267c44e
msgid "Nav sidebar is half-Chinese, half-English"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md 2a5839e1885141bb97df2032fe8684f4
msgid ""
"Maintain `h1_map.zh_CN.yml` and gate CI on its completeness for any "
"chapter whose `zh_status` is `required`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md 6251dde2a01142c884ead7bdbbc7e4dc
msgid "Machine translation silently approved"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md 4d20ae6efd5f4d7593b913e5ae5b250e
msgid "Chinese reader sees nonsense"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md ebbf10e01e03494d9f8ce3b526f798fa
msgid ""
"Every machine-translated `msgstr` lands as `fuzzy`; the `fuzzy` flag must"
" be cleared by a human."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:238
#: 1784817573144598ba9e677dd175c74b
msgid ""
"Each of these is a one-line rule; the appendix's point is that they are "
"not optional if the bilingual publishing is to stay trustworthy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:241
#: 1b2618ad860645249d65d584aa2c917a
msgid "Keep it simple"
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:243
#: c73eb95bcd334bfea29364bb0af9ae6d
msgid ""
"The full discipline above fits comfortably in a few hundred lines of "
"configuration, a small `h1_map` file per language, and a one-line check. "
"It does not require a translation management system, a separate content "
"repository, or a parallel prose tree. It does require the four "
"disciplines above to be in place from the first day of bilingual "
"publishing — the failure modes all become expensive to fix retroactively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../appendix-e-bilingual-publishing.md:251
#: a3ee8a3467f74cdfadf66ac661f69b6e
msgid ""
"The rest is routine Sphinx workflow: `make book-i18n` to refresh, `make "
"book-build -D language=zh_CN` to render, CI to enforce the `zh_status` "
"hard gate. Nothing in this appendix needs new tooling; everything needs "
"the disciplines to be named and enforced."
msgstr ""

